        "regex": "",
        "description": "Instance picker. Driven off command_delivery_claims_lost_total, which is a LABEL VECTOR (path=sweep|nudge) and would therefore export nothing until the first lost claim -- so the processor pre-initialises both paths at zero at registration, which is what keeps this picker able to name an instance on a healthy install. Do not repoint it at a counter that is not pre-initialised: the batch counters are the example, empty until the first fleet write."
