  "timezone": "",
  "title": "DeviceChain \u2014 Command Delivery",
  "uid": "dc-command-delivery-ops",
  "description": "Operations board for command delivery: fleet writes (batch enqueues, device dispositions, refusal codes and whether the delivery-machinery reserve caused them, cancels), the claim outcomes of both dispatch paths (the periodic sweep and the enqueue-time nudge), and the presence gate's holds. The instance picker is driven by claims_lost rather than by a batch counter, because the batch counters are label vectors that export nothing until the first fleet write \u2014 picking one of those would leave the dashboard unable to name an instance that has only ever sent single commands. claims_lost is a label vector too, since the sweep and the nudge are counted apart, so the processor PRE-INITIALISES both paths at zero at registration; that is what keeps it usable here, and it is why repointing this at any counter without the same treatment would reintroduce the empty-picker problem. Note the two naming eras: the six original counters carry a historical command_delivery_ stutter in their metric names and the batch counters do not.",
  "version": 1,
  "weekStart": "",
  "panels": [
    {
      "id": 1,
      "type": "row",
      "title": "Fleet writes",
      "collapsed": false,
